---
title: Pork Chops with Peach Salsa
course: main
servings: 4
time_active: 30
time_total: 40
leftovers: good
tags: [weeknight]
pairs: [crispy-rosemary-fingerlings]
description: Spiced, butter-basted pork chops served over a bright peach and jalapeño salsa.
---

== Salsa ==

Dice @peaches{2}(ripe; or 1 mango), @red bell pepper{1/2}, and @red onion{1/4}. Seed and mince @jalapeño{1}.

Toss with @cilantro{1/2%bunch}(chopped), the juice of a @lime{1}, and a pinch of @salt. Add a small drizzle of @?honey{} if the fruit isn't very sweet. Let it sit while you cook the chops.

== Pork Chops ==

Pat @pork chops{4}(bone-in, about 1 inch thick) dry. Season generously with @salt, @black pepper{}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @cumin{1/2%tsp}, and @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}. Let them sit at room temperature for ~{20%minutes}.

Heat a drizzle of @olive oil{} in a #cast iron skillet{} over medium-high. Sear the chops without moving them until deeply browned, ~{4-5%minutes} per side.

In the last minute, add @butter{1%tbsp} and spoon it over the chops. Pull them at 140°F; they'll rise to 145°F as they rest.

Rest ~{5%minutes}. Spoon the salsa onto each plate, lay a chop on top, and pour the resting juices over it. Serve with wedges of @?lime{1}.

> For a light glaze, brush a little honey on the chops with the butter in the last minute. Watch closely, since honey burns fast.
